@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995 (חוק הביטוח הלאומי), ss 342 and 348 and
-- Schedule K. THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module of this row imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt,
-- Hebrew Wikisource raw MediaWiki, retrieved 2026-10-06, sha256 78bf47ee...2a97. An unofficial
-- consolidation of the text as amended at retrieval. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of that file,
-- generated by row IL-04's tools/srcquote.py (run by path, not copied); nothing in Hebrew here is
-- typed by hand.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS), as a bare NUMBER.
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the fact, or a
-- register, a return, an employer's payroll or the Institute's records hold it. Whether the fact
-- makes contributions payable, by whom, and on what income, is a rule, and belongs in the module of
-- the provision that says so.

§ `Nouns for sections 342 and 348 and Schedule K`

§§ `Declared again from row IL-04, with the same names`

-- Row IL-04 declares these two types in ../legalese-2026-10-il-04/nii-il04-nouns.l4. This row was
-- to IMPORT them, but the l4 binary resolves an IMPORT by bare module name beside the importing
-- file, so a module in a sibling directory is not found (tested 2026-10-06; NOTES.md section 8).
-- They are declared again here, constructor for constructor, so that at IL-07 this copy can be
-- deleted in favour of IL-04's without renaming anything that uses them.
--
-- The nine branches of insurance, in the order Schedule J prints them (its items 1 and 2 are both
-- maternity). s 335 imposes contributions branch by branch, and s 342(c)(1) names the deduction by
-- the s 335 subsections, which map onto branches (NOTES.md, fork F12).
DECLARE `A branch of insurance` IS ONE OF
    `maternity`
    `children`
    `work injury`
    `accident injury`
    `unemployment`
    `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`
    `disability`
    `long-term care`
    `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Who the insured person is, in the three-way split of Schedule J's column C. Which of the three a
-- person is follows from the s 1 definitions (row IL-04 encodes them) and from s 334(b).
DECLARE `A column of insured persons in Schedule J` IS ONE OF
    `an employee`
    `a self-employed person`
    `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`

-- Version 0.3.0: row IL-04's reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ
-- (IL-04's fork F4; ruled by Meng on 2026-10-07: the printed totals govern by default, the items'
-- reading kept as the alternative). Declared again, constructor for constructor, for the same reason
-- as the two types above. It is an argument of the s 342 rules that take one, never a field of the
-- case records, so that records built before 0.3.0 (tests-independent.l4's included) still build.
DECLARE `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ` IS ONE OF
    `the printed totals govern`
    `the items govern`

§§ `Periods: the tax year, its quarters and its months`

-- Schedule K defines the quarter:
-- src:4771 | ”רבעון“ – תקופה של שלושה חודשים רצופים המתחילה ב־1 בינואר, ב־1 באפריל, ב־1 ביולי או ב־1 באוקטובר של כל שנת מס;
-- A tax year is a calendar year here (s 1 "שנת מס" points to the Income Tax Ordinance, whose
-- special assessment periods are not modelled; row IL-04's fork F12).
DECLARE `A quarter of a tax year` IS ONE OF
    `the quarter beginning on 1 January`
    `the quarter beginning on 1 April`
    `the quarter beginning on 1 July`
    `the quarter beginning on 1 October`

-- Schedule K states figures "לחודש" (for a month, item 1 only), "לרבעון" (for a quarter) and "לשנה"
-- (for a year). A month is numbered 1 for January to 12 for December.
DECLARE `A period under Schedule K` IS ONE OF
    `a month of the tax year` HAS `the month` IS A NUMBER
    `a quarter of the tax year` HAS `the quarter` IS A `A quarter of a tax year`
    `the whole tax year`

§§ `The items of Schedule K`

-- src:4757 | פרט | בעד | הכנסה מרבית | הכנסה מזערית |
-- Column "בעד" (for whom) names four kinds of insured person. Which item applies to a person is a
-- rule (nii-s348-maximum-minimum.l4); the four items are the schedule's own structure.
DECLARE `An item of Schedule K` IS ONE OF
    `item 1, an employee`
    `item 2, a self-employed person`
    `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)`
    `item 4, another insured person`

§§ `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`

-- Schedule K is written in terms of three figures the Law computes elsewhere and does not print:
-- "the basic amount" (paragraph (3) of the s 1 definition, updated each 1 January), "the average
-- wage" of a month (s 1, updated on each "update day": 1 January and the first of any month in which
-- compensation applies), and "the minimum wage" applicable to the particular employee (the Minimum
-- Wage Law). Each is a published fact; nii-il05-published-figures.l4 has the 2026 figures.
--
-- An update of the average wage after 1 January of the tax year, on the first day of the month it
-- names. INPUT CONVENTION: updates are listed in order of month, at most one per month.
DECLARE `An update of the average wage within the tax year` HAS
    `the month of the update`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the average wage as updated`                                         IS A NUMBER

-- INPUT CONVENTIONS:
-- * `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` is the basic amount in force
--   in the tax year. s 1 updates it only on 1 January (the update clause, paragraph (2), source line
--   196), so one figure serves the whole year.
-- * which average wage: the figure "for contributions". s 2(b) changes the calculation of the average
--   wage "for benefits and contributions"; NOTES.md fork F1 says which figure this row's tests supply
--   and why.
DECLARE `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year` HAS
    `tax year`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the basic amount under paragraph (3) of its definition in section 1` IS A NUMBER
    `the average wage as updated on 1 January`                            IS A NUMBER
    `later updates of the average wage in the tax year`                   IS A LIST OF `An update of the average wage within the tax year`

-- "minimum wage" in Schedule K is the minimum wage, partial minimum wage, daily or hourly minimum wage
-- "applicable, as the case may be, under the Minimum Wage Law to a particular employee":
-- src:4772 | ”שכר מינימום“ – שכר מינימום, שכר מינימום חלקי, שכר מינימום יומי, או שכר מינימום לשעה החל, לפי הענין, לפי הוראות חוק שכר מינימום לגבי עובד פלוני;
-- So it belongs to the employee, not to the year: a part-time employee's figure is the partial
-- minimum wage. Item 1 reads it for "the first month of the quarter", so four figures a year, each the
-- monthly amount for that month (a daily or hourly rate converted to the month by the Minimum Wage
-- Law, which is not in this row).
DECLARE `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter` HAS
    `in January`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `in April`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `in July`                                                             IS A NUMBER
    `in October`                                                          IS A NUMBER

§§ `An insured person's period, for section 348`

-- The case for s 348. INPUT CONVENTIONS, each because the rule that settles it is outside this row:
-- * `column`: employee, self-employed or neither (s 1 and s 334(b); row IL-04).
-- * `income from work in the period`: income as an employee (s 344, monthly) or as a self-employed
--   person (s 345, annual, or its share of the period), after every provision outside this row that
--   says what counts. Not negative.
-- * `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`: income from the sources in
--   s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance that is not income from work as an employee or as a
--   self-employed person, less whatever s 350 exempts. s 348(a1) disregards part of it. Not negative.
-- * `the minimum wage applicable to the employee`: for an employee, the Schedule K "minimum wage"
--   (above); NOTHING for one who is not an employee.
-- * `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`: s 348(d); the Institute's
--   records show it. Stated for a month.
-- * The four s 348(e) classes are statuses a register holds (the national service or civil service
--   administration, the yeshiva's certificate). The national-civic service one is a date, because the
--   temporary text reaches only those who began before 31.8.2026: the day the person began serving,
--   if the person serves in it in the period; NOTHING if not.
-- * `section 350(c) disapplies section 348(b) to the person`: s 350(c) (source line 3805, not in this
--   row) says s 348(b) does not apply to a resident exempt under s 350(a) whose other income is nil
--   or below the minimum. Whether it reaches the person is s 350's question; the Institute records it.
-- * `an order under section 348(c) has changed a minimum amount for the period`: s 348(c) lets the
--   Minister change the minimum amounts by order; no order is in the sources, so where one reaches
--   the period the rules decline.
-- src:3805 | (ג) הוראות סעיף 348(ב) לא יחולו לגבי תושב ישראל כאמור בסעיף קטן (א) שאין לו הכנסה אחרת מלבד ההכנסה שהוא פטור לגביה לפי אותו סעיף קטן או שיש לו הכנסה אחרת כאמור שאינה מגיעה לסכום המזערי האמור לגביו בלוח י״א.
DECLARE `An insured person's period under section 348` HAS
    `tax year`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `period`                                                              IS A `A period under Schedule K`
    `column`                                                              IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
    `income from work in the period`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`    IS A NUMBER
    `the minimum wage applicable to the employee`                         IS A MAYBE `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
    `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a volunteer in national service or in community volunteering`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a student in a Torah institution or in a yeshiva`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `serving in civil service as defined in section 6(a) of the Deferral of Service for Yeshiva Students Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the person began national-civic service, if serving in it`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `section 350(c) disapplies section 348(b) to the person`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `an order under section 348(c) has changed a minimum amount for the period` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `An order changing the minimum amounts, for section 348(c)`

-- src:3766 | (ג) השר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות בצו את הסכומים המזעריים האמורים בלוח י״א.
DECLARE `An order changing the minimum amounts in Schedule K` HAS
    `made by the Minister`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`                    IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)`

-- s 342(a) excepts "an insured woman under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured
-- person". Chapter C (maternity insurance) is not in this row; the Institute's records show on what
-- footing a woman is insured.
DECLARE `An insured person, for section 342(a)-(b)` HAS
    `column`                                                              IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
    `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Version 0.4.0 (05-P3). s 342(f) speaks of "an employee who is also self-employed" (source line
-- 3673), whom (b) reaches as an employee and (a) as self-employed. The record above has one column,
-- so such a person took two calls; this one takes both statuses. Neither TRUE is one who is neither.
DECLARE `An insured person who may be both an employee and self-employed, for section 342(a)-(b)` HAS
    `works as an employee`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `works as a self-employed person`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `insured under Chapter C only, by virtue of being the wife of an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Who s 342(a)-(b) makes liable. The third member is the source's own named absence: "is not liable".
DECLARE `The person liable to pay the contributions under section 342` IS ONE OF
    `the employer, for the employee`
    `the insured person, for himself`
    `no one: an insured woman under Chapter C only, as the wife of an insured person, is not liable`

§§ `An employee's month, for section 342(c)`

-- The amount Schedule J's column D gives for one branch on the employee's wage: the column D
-- percentages applied to the parts of the wage, which is Schedule J's arithmetic and row IL-04's
-- (`the column D deduction under` in its nii-schedule-j.l4). It enters here as an input because that
-- module cannot be imported (NOTES.md section 8).
DECLARE `A branch's column D amount` HAS
    `branch`                                                              IS A `A branch of insurance`
    `amount`                                                              IS A NUMBER

-- s 342(c)(2): "for the time for which a senior citizen pension is payable to the insured", where
-- "senior citizen pension" includes a special senior citizen benefit. For a month, the pension is
-- payable for all of it, part of it, or none of it.
DECLARE `The senior citizen pension in the month` IS ONE OF
    `payable for the whole month`
    `payable for part of the month`
    `not payable for any of the month`

-- s 342(c)(2)'s age limb: 70 for a man; for a woman, "the age fixed for her by her month of birth in
-- Part D of Schedule A1". Part D is a table outside this row that gives the age in years and months;
-- it enters here in months (65 and 4 months is 784).
DECLARE `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a man`
    `a woman` HAS `the age fixed for her by her month of birth in Part D of Schedule A1, in months` IS A NUMBER

-- Version 0.5.0 (fork DATE; BACKLOG IL-39). The date of birth moved on by the age can fall on a day
-- the month lacks (29 February in a common year; the 31st in a month of 30 days or fewer), and the
-- text does not say what day that is. Three readings, kept by name. Ruled by Meng on 2026-10-08
-- (SHRUG): declined by default. A reading is an argument, never a field of the case records.
DECLARE `A reading of a day of birth the month of the age lacks` IS ONE OF
    `the last day of that month`
    `the first day of the next month`
    `such a day is declined`

-- The case for s 342(c). INPUT CONVENTIONS:
-- * `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`: s 335's answer (row IL-04's
--   convention; s 335 is not in this row or IL-04's).
-- * `the column D amounts on the wage`: one entry per branch, from Schedule J (above). Version 0.4.0
--   (05-RC2): s 342(c)(1) takes "percentages of the income on which the contributions are payable"
--   (source line 3661), so these are amounts on the wage as s 348(a) takes it into account, not
--   above the Schedule K maximum. The s 342 rules that read them cannot check that; the forms "…
--   from a wage of" (nii-s342-liability-and-deduction.l4) apply s 348(a) themselves.
-- * `a police officer or a prison officer`: within the meaning of the Police Law (Disabled and Fallen)
--   or the Prison Service Law (Disabled and Fallen), which s 342(c)(2) cites; a matter of record.
-- * `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section
--   342(e)(4)`: those regulations (5757-1997, noted at source line 3671) and approvals are not in the
--   sources; where one governs the deduction, the s 342(c) rules decline.
DECLARE `An employee's month under section 342(c)` HAS
    `tax year`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `month`                                                               IS A NUMBER
    `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
    `the column D amounts on the wage`                                    IS A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`  @desc column D, branch by branch, on the wage as section 348(a) takes it into account (not above the Schedule K maximum); the rules that read these amounts cannot check it, and those "from a wage of" or "on a total monthly income of" compute them from the wage (05-RC2)
    `senior citizen pension`                                             IS A `The senior citizen pension in the month`
    `the insured person`                                                  IS A `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)`
    `date of birth`                                                       IS A DATE
    `a police officer or a prison officer`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Several employers, for section 342(d)`

-- s 342(d) compares "the actual deduction" with "the coordinated contributions" and names two
-- outcomes; when they are equal it names none, and when there is one employer it does not apply.
DECLARE `The outcome of section 342(d)` IS ONE OF
    `the employee pays the difference`                                    HAS `the difference` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee is entitled to a refund of the difference`             HAS `the difference` IS A NUMBER
    `neither paragraph: the actual deduction equals the coordinated contributions`
    `section 342(d) does not apply: the insured person works for one employer`

§§ `A renewed kibbutz member's month, for section 342(e1)`

-- s 342(e1) turns on s 3A(a) and (b) (not in this row) and on what the member's other employer
-- deducted. INPUT CONVENTION: `the member's month, as if paid by one employer` is the s 342(c) case
-- for the member's total monthly income; the coordinated contributions are computed from it.
DECLARE `A renewed kibbutz member's month under section 342(e1)` HAS
    `meets section 3A(a)`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `works as stated in section 3A(b)`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member's month, as if paid by one employer`                      IS AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
    `contributions deducted for the member's wage by the other employer for the month` IS A NUMBER

§§ `An employee who is also self-employed, for section 342(f)`

-- s 342(f) speaks of income by its source in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance: s 2(1) business or
-- vocation and s 2(8) (the self-employed person's income), and s 2(2) employment. Amounts for the
-- month; not negative.
DECLARE `An employee who is also self-employed, in a month` HAS
    `tax year`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `month`                                                               IS A NUMBER
    `income from the sources in sections 2(1) and 2(8) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month` IS A NUMBER
    `income from the sources in section 2(2) of the Income Tax Ordinance in the month` IS A NUMBER
